(6886456, 1037568, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Absolutely *LOVE* the lighting that illuminates the beauty of the trees. I can almost hear the sway of the jewel like leaves waving in the breeze. Top notch work.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Absolutely *LOVE* the lighting that illuminates the beauty of the trees. I can almost hear the sway of the jewel like leaves waving in the breeze. Top notch work.', '2012-10-19 18:25:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6886459, 1037435, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Great B&amp;W tones in this composition. The sky takes on a moody almost rainy day aspect. The tall tree seems to lean in towards the mountain view beckoning us to come forth to take in the view and seek shelter from the weather.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Great B&W tones in this composition. The sky takes on a moody almost rainy day aspect. The tall tree seems to lean in towards the mountain view beckoning us to come forth to take in the view and seek shelter from the weather.', '2012-10-19 18:28:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6886461, 1036845, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Beautiful abstract of the autumn gold that adorns the trees. Love the simple lines and the rich warm golden hues that captures the attention. The lines and the gold ''dots'' gives this composition texture - it is almost like brush strokes on a painting. Nicely done.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Beautiful abstract of the autumn gold that adorns the trees. Love the simple lines and the rich warm golden hues that captures the attention. The lines and the gold ''dots'' gives this composition texture - it is almost like brush strokes on a painting. Nicely done.', '2012-10-19 18:31:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6886462, 1037450, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>I wish that you were able to capture all of the autumn color tree (the full trunk) but it may be because it is so hard to isolate just a single tree without introducing distracting elements. What makes this shot so spectacular for me is that gorgeous light that makes those leaves sparkle with gold, red-orange, and green light. Kudos to you for capturing the beauty of the tree in spectacular light.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. I wish that you were able to capture all of the autumn color tree (the full trunk) but it may be because it is so hard to isolate just a single tree without introducing distracting elements. What makes this shot so spectacular for me is that gorgeous light that makes those leaves sparkle with gold, red-orange, and green light. Kudos to you for capturing the beauty of the tree in spectacular light.', '2012-10-19 18:34:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6886464, 1037504, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Love the leading lines and shadow of the fence that act as a path to lead my eye to the tree at the end. Lovely autumn colors can be seen dressing up the greens of the tree. It is a great composition, but I do have two small critiques. First off I think that the composition could be even stronger if it was composed on the vertical - the reasons are that it would follow the vertical lines of the shadow and complement the vertical line orientation of the main tree. Not to mention it would eliminate the elements on the far right and left that do nothing to add to the scene. Lastly, I think the one stop resizing robbed some of the sharpness and detail of the large photo. You could get that back by sharpening twice (the minimal rules do allow that) Nonetheless, very beautiful and well scene shot.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Love the leading lines and shadow of the fence that act as a path to lead my eye to the tree at the end. Lovely autumn colors can be seen dressing up the greens of the tree. It is a great composition, but I do have two small critiques. First off I think that the composition could be even stronger if it was composed on the vertical - the reasons are that it would follow the vertical lines of the shadow and complement the vertical line orientation of the main tree. Not to mention it would eliminate the elements on the far right and left that do nothing to add to the scene. Lastly, I think the one stop resizing robbed some of the sharpness and detail of the large photo. You could get that back by sharpening twice (the minimal rules do allow that) Nonetheless, very beautiful and well scene shot.', '2012-10-19 18:46:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6886529, 1037481, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Love the blanket of gold and orange on the forest floor. The detail in the bark of the tree trunks is great. Off in the distance I can see the lovely trees with leafy foliage that mimics the forest floor.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Love the blanket of gold and orange on the forest floor. The detail in the bark of the tree trunks is great. Off in the distance I can see the lovely trees with leafy foliage that mimics the forest floor.', '2012-10-19 21:22:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6886536, 1037101, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Heh, something a little different to spruce up the trees;-) Points for the humor factor...I still would have loved to see more of the lovely autumn colors on the trees but I get it that they are the supporting cast in this composition. Oh, and I''d much rather have the humor of a storm trooper on a speeder bike than an ewok:-)</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Heh, something a little different to spruce up the trees;-) Points for the humor factor...I still would have loved to see more of the lovely autumn colors on the trees but I get it that they are the supporting cast in this composition. Oh, and I''d much rather have the humor of a storm trooper on a speeder bike than an ewok:-)', '2012-10-19 21:26:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6886540, 1037584, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>The composition of having the two aspens grow out of the bottom corners and stretch to the sky makes me, the view feel very small indeed in the presence of this two trees. The white trunks really contrast boldly off of the blue sky. My only critique is that I wish that those two trees could be the only elements in the composition, but I''m sure that it was nearly impossible to find trees that were remote from other things (I found that to be challenging myself in shooting for this challenge)</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. The composition of having the two aspens grow out of the bottom corners and stretch to the sky makes me, the view feel very small indeed in the presence of this two trees. The white trunks really contrast boldly off of the blue sky. My only critique is that I wish that those two trees could be the only elements in the composition, but I''m sure that it was nearly impossible to find trees that were remote from other things (I found that to be challenging myself in shooting for this challenge)', '2012-10-19 21:30:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6886549, 1037510, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>This is a very different take on the trees challenge. It may not be the stunning beauty of landscapes but it does make you stop and think of the fuel to those nice, warm and toasty times hanging out near the fireplace. I wish the the light was better to illuminate and separate the axe from the firewood in the backdrop. Something as simple as a flashlight, a longer exposure and someone to shine the light up &amp; down <u>on the back</u> of the axe &amp; handle would have made the axe standout from the backdrop. I do like how you have a dramatic spotlight on the tree stump that holds the axe but the rest of the composition the lighting falls a bit flat. I wonder what this looks like in color and if it would have been better visually over the B&amp;W tones.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. This is a very different take on the trees challenge. It may not be the stunning beauty of landscapes but it does make you stop and think of the fuel to those nice, warm and toasty times hanging out near the fireplace. I wish the the light was better to illuminate and separate the axe from the firewood in the backdrop. Something as simple as a flashlight, a longer exposure and someone to shine the light up & down on the back of the axe & handle would have made the axe standout from the backdrop. I do like how you have a dramatic spotlight on the tree stump that holds the axe but the rest of the composition the lighting falls a bit flat. I wonder what this looks like in color and if it would have been better visually over the B&W tones.', '2012-10-19 21:41:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6886558, 1037449, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Grats on finding a single tree that can be isolated from the backdrop. Wonderful find and a very lovely tree. This tree dominates the composition and captivates the viewer''s eye. I just love those red-gold leaves sparkle like jewels as they catch the light. I also like the low angle you took this at in that it grows out from the bottom left and reaches for the sky as it bends up and out to the top of the frame.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Grats on finding a single tree that can be isolated from the backdrop. Wonderful find and a very lovely tree. This tree dominates the composition and captivates the viewer''s eye. I just love those red-gold leaves sparkle like jewels as they catch the light. I also like the low angle you took this at in that it grows out from the bottom left and reaches for the sky as it bends up and out to the top of the frame.', '2012-10-19 21:48:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6886567, 1037089, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment and bump up.<br/> <br/>Love the soft muted light captured here - makes me think of a a soft and warm breeze as the sun sets on a day that was well spent by the water. The tree does indeed seem to be leaning towards the sunset and it is the perfect invitation to go lean upon the strong trunk and watch the sun set over the water. Very lovely and nicely composed.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment and bump up. Love the soft muted light captured here - makes me think of a a soft and warm breeze as the sun sets on a day that was well spent by the water. The tree does indeed seem to be leaning towards the sunset and it is the perfect invitation to go lean upon the strong trunk and watch the sun set over the water. Very lovely and nicely composed.', '2012-10-19 21:58:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6886599, 1037308, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>This is definitely a beautiful place to take a stroll. The dirt road acts as a leading line that draws the eye in to travel along the path of trees that line the edge.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. This is definitely a beautiful place to take a stroll. The dirt road acts as a leading line that draws the eye in to travel along the path of trees that line the edge.', '2012-10-19 22:54:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6886604, 1037367, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Those trees look like they are standing in salute to the flag. The shot has high potential but it needs a few things to strengthen the composition. First off I am guessing that the original file size was large - any time you have to take it down to a small file size it loses sharpness and detail. Minimal editing doesn''t allow a two resize down but it does allow for sharpening twice (or more if you wish but then you run the risk of oversharpening). Second, I think the composition would be stronger if you composed it on a vertical to follow and complement the vertical lines of the trees and the flag pole. Also if it was possible a zoom (I realize sometimes you have to work with what equipment you have and/or cannot get physically closer) in to bring us closer to the main subject always is a bonus. Lastly, the composition would be stronger if the flag was blowing in the wind. Maybe you could have waited for that moment...then again maybe Mother Nature was refusing to cooperate and unfurl the flag for you.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Those trees look like they are standing in salute to the flag. The shot has high potential but it needs a few things to strengthen the composition. First off I am guessing that the original file size was large - any time you have to take it down to a small file size it loses sharpness and detail. Minimal editing doesn''t allow a two resize down but it does allow for sharpening twice (or more if you wish but then you run the risk of oversharpening). Second, I think the composition would be stronger if you composed it on a vertical to follow and complement the vertical lines of the trees and the flag pole. Also if it was possible a zoom (I realize sometimes you have to work with what equipment you have and/or cannot get physically closer) in to bring us closer to the main subject always is a bonus. Lastly, the composition would be stronger if the flag was blowing in the wind. Maybe you could have waited for that moment...then again maybe Mother Nature was refusing to cooperate and unfurl the flag for you.', '2012-10-19 23:02:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6886611, 1037592, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Great details in the tree trunk and the leaves. Composition is good but has potential to be stellar. I think better lighting would have been better for it could have introduced a dramatic element to the composition. I.e. different times of the day illuminate the leaves to give it a natural glow or the sun lights up the side of the trunk to give some drama in highlights and shadow. Just a suggestion but another idea that could have been added to get a little more visual appeal is to have one leaf ''falling'' in the frame. Admittingly, the attempt would be far more difficult to capture both tree and leaf in sharp detail but it may be possible if a leaf is held just at the top of the frame, focused on and let go with shutter fired.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Great details in the tree trunk and the leaves. Composition is good but has potential to be stellar. I think better lighting would have been better for it could have introduced a dramatic element to the composition. I.e. different times of the day illuminate the leaves to give it a natural glow or the sun lights up the side of the trunk to give some drama in highlights and shadow. Just a suggestion but another idea that could have been added to get a little more visual appeal is to have one leaf ''falling'' in the frame. Admittingly, the attempt would be far more difficult to capture both tree and leaf in sharp detail but it may be possible if a leaf is held just at the top of the frame, focused on and let go with shutter fired.', '2012-10-19 23:21:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6886691, 1037521, 153814, '<td valign="top">This is one of my favotites. I like the blend of colors<br/>The green grass mixed with the leaves is great.<br/>The yellow tree is a great complement to the foreground.<br/>Buy that slanted house I could do without.</td>', 'This is one of my favotites. I like the blend of colorsThe green grass mixed with the leaves is great.The yellow tree is a great complement to the foreground.Buy that slanted house I could do without.', '2012-10-20 07:18:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6886693, 1037584, 153814, '<td valign="top">Nice perspective and contrast.<br/>One of my top picks.<br/>The sky looks a tad grainy but it could be my monitor<br/>so I didn''t hold it against the photo.<br/>Very nice.</td>', 'Nice perspective and contrast.One of my top picks.The sky looks a tad grainy but it could be my monitorso I didn''t hold it against the photo.Very nice.', '2012-10-20 07:23:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6886694, 1037116, 153814, '<td valign="top">You can''t go wrong with a palm tree shot &amp; this one has the <br/>added bonus of the amazing colors in the sky.<br/>I just wish you didn''t clip off the right edge of the first palm.<br/>All in all very nice.</td>', 'You can''t go wrong with a palm tree shot & this one has the added bonus of the amazing colors in the sky.I just wish you didn''t clip off the right edge of the first palm.All in all very nice.', '2012-10-20 07:26:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6886695, 1037476, 153814, '<td valign="top">I usually don''t like landscapes or nature that isn''t done in color<br/>BUT this works. This shot has everything. Trees, water, tall grass, sky, clouds, birds, and if that isn''t enough we have the floating dog house to <br/>figure out. Yet with all that going on I''m still drawn to that huge tree.<br/>Very nice.</td>', 'I usually don''t like landscapes or nature that isn''t done in colorBUT this works. This shot has everything. Trees, water, tall grass, sky, clouds, birds, and if that isn''t enough we have the floating dog house to figure out. Yet with all that going on I''m still drawn to that huge tree.Very nice.', '2012-10-20 07:35:21.000000', NULL, 1),
